    "body": "<p>Learn how to create and send a WhatsApp campaign in Klaviyo. WhatsApp campaigns use approved message templates and allow you to include structured content such as headers, bodies, footers, and buttons.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KHS824Q0STHAPHTE1B0RXVG0\">What is a WhatsApp campaign?</h2>\n<p>A WhatsApp campaign is a one-time message sent to a list or segment of subscribers. You can use campaigns to announce product launches, promote sales, or share important updates. You can send a campaign immediately or schedule it for a future time.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KHS824Q0H4PS0K47ESNZCC8B\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>Before sending a WhatsApp campaign, you must have:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Connected and configured WhatsApp in your Klaviyo account</li>\n<li>Collected explicit WhatsApp marketing consent</li>\n<li>An approved WhatsApp message template</li>\n</ul>\n<p>WhatsApp requires all outbound marketing messages to use pre-approved templates. Learn how template approval works, message structure, and character limits in <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/40116644987675\">WhatsApp message templates </a>.</p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>As of April 1, 2025, Meta will block WhatsApp marketing messages sent to US phone numbers. Delivered to US recipients will fail with the error code 131049.</p>\n</div>\n<p>You should also have a list or segment of subscribers who have opted in to receive WhatsApp marketing.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01KHS824Q0NC8XCMM205DKFCBX\">Campaigns vs. flows</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%\"><strong>Campaigns</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%\"><strong>Flows</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>One-time sends that are manually scheduled</td>\n<td>Automated and ongoing sends</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sent to a specific list or segment</td>\n<td>Triggered by customer actions or profile properties</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Best for announcements and promotions</td>\n<td>Best for lifecycle messaging and automation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KHS824Q0VWJ8W08PZMWCVC70\">Create a WhatsApp campaign</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to the <strong>Campaigns</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create campaign</strong> in the upper right.</li>\n<li>Name your campaign.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>WhatsApp</strong> as the campaign type.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Continue</strong>.</li>\n<li>Under <em>Audience</em>, select the list(s) or segment(s) you want to send to.<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>To exclude specific groups, add a segment under <em>Don't send to</em>.</li>\n<li>Turn on Smart Sending to avoid messaging subscribers too frequently.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select an approved WhatsApp template.</li>\n<li>Customize the template fields:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Header</strong> (optional)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Body</strong> (required)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Footer</strong> (optional)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Buttons</strong> (optional)</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Add links in the body of the message when possible. Links placed in the body are automatically tracked by Klaviyo.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Preview &amp; test</strong> to preview the message as a specific profile.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</li>\n<li>On the review page, confirm that:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>The correct audience is selected.</li>\n<li>Your template variables are populated correctly.</li>\n<li>Your account has sufficient credits.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Schedule or Send</strong>.</li>\n<li>Choose whether to send immediately or schedule for a future date and time.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Schedule</strong> or <strong>Send Now</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>WhatsApp campaigns are subject to Meta delivery policies. Large sends may be rate limited depending on your WhatsApp sending tier.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01KHS824Q0KT0N4TWRVEAR56KV\">Best times and days to send</h2>\n<p>The best time to send depends on your audience. Test different days and times to determine what drives the highest engagement.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Weekday campaigns often drive higher revenue.</li>\n<li>Early afternoon and early evening typically produce higher engagement.</li>\n</ul>",
